# Repo root = this folder (the add-on package). The dev workspace one level up
# -- CLAUDE.md, docs/, releases/, every dev_*.py -- is deliberately OUTSIDE the
# repo. The "public repo scope" block below is a safety net for a file that
# lands in here by mistake: the shared rules (§2) want it in every Sculptools
# repo, and it costs nothing.
#
# Everything tracked here is shipped in the zip, with one intentional exception:
# images/ is tracked (GitHub renders the README banner from it) but excluded
# from the zip by dev_build.py. Do not "fix" that asymmetry in either direction.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Blender
*.blend1
*.blend2
*.blend@

# Extension build artifacts
*.zip

# OS / editor
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Scratch / temp
/scratch/
/tmp/

# -- Public repo scope -------------------------------------------------
# The GitHub repo holds ONLY the add-on package (what ships in the zip),
# plus images/ for the README banner. Never committed:
#   - project docs, AI context and handoff notes
#   - dev-only test / probe / build scripts (every one is named dev_*.py)
#   - build artifacts (release zips)
/docs/
/validation/
/releases/
/release/
/dev_*.py
CLAUDE.md
STORE_LISTING.md
handoff.md
